{"id": "EUVD-2026-96373", "enisaUuid": "a6aaf67b-6b7d-3fc6-8f94-9bdc2281cbf0", "description": "1MCP Agent (@1mcp/agent) 0.20.0 through 0.39.0 contains an incorrect authorization vulnerability that allows authenticated clients to bypass OAuth tag-scope enforcement using negated advanced tag-filter expressions. Attackers holding a single-tag token can send a filter like not <granted-tag> to list and invoke tools on backend MCP servers outside their granted scopes.", "datePublished": "2026-10-10T16:14:10", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-13T18:27:18", "baseScore": 5.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:L/VI:L/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@haind/1mcp-negated-tag-filter-oauth-scope-bypass", "https://github.com/1mcp-app/agent/blob/v0.39.0/src/sdk/legacy/transport/http/middlewares/scopeAuthMiddleware.ts#L163-L183", "https://github.com/1mcp-app/agent/blob/v0.39.0/src/transport/http/routes/inspectHelpers.ts#L79-L102", "https://github.com/1mcp-app/agent", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/1mcp-agent-0.20.0-through-0.39.0-oauth-tag-scope-bypass-via-negated-tag-filter"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-108586", "GHSA-w2j7-xxh9-9q67"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.19, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "108c7377-56d4-3cbb-bfb8-71791db7b40c", "product": {"name": "@1mcp/agent", "vendor": {"name": "1mcp-app"}}, "product_version": "0.20.0 \u22640.39.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "5ca3877e-9da6-3789-abb0-bf67df02016e", "vendor": {"name": "1mcp-app"}}], "isExploited": false}